      "id": "book-mountainous-miscellany",
      "slug": "book-mountainous-miscellany",
      "title": "Mountainous Miscellany",
      "region": "liyue",
      "category": "books-literature",
      "classification": "canon",
      "summary": "Mountainous Miscellany is a quest text that gives a dusk-time clue for finding Subrosium near Mt. Tianheng and records a local belief about the stone.",
      "body": [
        "Mountainous Miscellany is a quest item found during Bygones Times Like Dust Passing, part of Interlude Chapter: Act I — The Crane Returns on the Wind. It is a short text about Subrosium, a stone connected in local belief with Mt. Tianheng.",
        "The note says Subrosium can be found at the right place and time: stand in the middle of the lake south of Mt. Tianheng at dusk and look toward the setting sun. It adds that some people believe the stone bridges the living and the dead.",
        "The quest uses the clue to lead the Traveler to the ore needed for the Jade Chamber’s Wonder Cores. The text records a legend and a practical location hint; it does not establish a general supernatural rule for Subrosium or explain the stone’s origin. The quest’s separate village records carry Shenhe’s family history."
      ],
