      "id": "book-robben-versus-chesterton-iridescent-brooch",
      "slug": "book-robben-versus-chesterton-iridescent-brooch",
      "title": "Robben versus Chesterton: Iridescent Brooch",
      "region": "fontaine",
      "category": "books-literature",
      "classification": "canon",
      "summary": "This three-volume Fontaine detective novel follows narrator Poiret and his uncle Chesterton as they investigate the Phantom Gentleman Fantomas Robben and the theft of an Iridescent Starstone Brooch. The collection explicitly calls itself fiction.",
      "body": [
        "Robben versus Chesterton: Iridescent Brooch is a three-volume Fontaine detective novel, and its description explicitly says the work is fictional. The story is narrated by Poiret, a young man who visits his detective uncle Chesterton and is drawn into an investigation of the Phantom Gentleman Fantomas Robben.",
        "The first volume stages a public theft of an Iridescent Starstone Brooch from a mansion during a blackout and explosion. The second reveals that the spectacle is a misdirection: Chesterton deduces that the brooch is still in the mansion and the explosion concealed a clockwork meka. In Volume III, Poiret considers whether Robben could be a group, before Chesterton turns the investigation on his supposed nephew and identifies him as Robben.",
        "The narrator’s name matches that of a detective assistant in Fontaine, but the books’ fiction disclaimer and the shared name alone do not establish that the novel’s Poiret and the in-game assistant are the same person."
      ],
